vectors) is checked by `cert/trace` only; `F` is its line `F`. Given a trace `T` with these
`d`, `n`, `F`, `poly_ok` is `checkPoly T cert = true` and `vanish` is `hvan` of
`check_mem_D_poly_presN` (TraceReplay/PolyVanish.lean) for `G = ⟨x | allRels⟩`. What the membership
claim then still rests on, outside the kernel: `check T members = true` (the trace; `cert/trace`),
the transcription of `F` and of the presentation's relators into `allRels` (this generator), `hsub`
(the trace's relators among `allRels`, `expandRel`), and `hord` (the test has `p`-power order in
`Δ/Δ^n`; GAP).
-/

